Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerVideo: output a waiting picture before asking for
 the next

A prepared start or resume retains its first picture in m_picture until
the preroll releases it. The release is followed by a resync, a priority
message; the next message is an ordinary packet, and its path asks the
decoder for the next picture straight into m_picture. The retained one
was released as dropped, never shown: the picture after it went out in
its slot, a frame early, and was then shown twice while the clock caught
up - one repeated frame at every start and resume.

Output a picture still waiting in m_picture before the decoder is asked
for the next one.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
@@ -682,6 +682,17 @@ void CVideoPlayerVideo::UpdatePlayerInfo
 
 bool CVideoPlayerVideo::ProcessDecoderOutput(double &frametime, double &pts)
 {
+  // A picture still waiting to be output goes first: asking the decoder for the
+  // next one overwrites it, and the codec releases what it held as dropped. The
+  // hold that retained it lets only priority messages through, but the resync
+  // that follows its release is one, and the packet after it lands here.
+  if (m_outputSate == OUTPUT_AGAIN && m_picture.videoBuffer)
+  {
+    m_outputSate = OutputPicture(&m_picture);
+    if (m_outputSate == OUTPUT_AGAIN)
+      return true;
+  }
+
   CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn decoderState = m_pVideoCodec->GetPicture(&m_picture);
 
   if (decoderState == CDVDVideoCodec::VC_BUFFER)
